  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 120 PM CDT Fri May 29 2026\n\nDry conditions will continue through the weekend. The ridge over the \narea will weaken allowing shortwaves energy to move across the area. \nThese shortwaves will interact with the afternoon seabreeze leading \nto a low (20-40%) chances of showers and thunderstorms each day \nstarting Monday. \n\nTemperatures in the 80s and 90s across South Texas will combine with \nabundant moisture resulting in heat index values of 100-105. Minor \nto moderate heat-related impacts are expected through next week.\n\nMinor coastal flooding chances appear lower than in previous \npackages as wave periods of 7 seconds or lower move into the area. \nWe will continue to monitor for water approaching the dunes as we \nnear the full moon.",
